caption: Word Affinities
tradition-component: word-affinities

When a Word is Good At an effect, it provides up to +2 to that Word’s roll for that effect. When it is Bad At an effect, it imposes up to -2 on that Word’s roll. The GM sets the modifier within that range according to how strongly the effect fits. A Forbidden effect cannot be produced with that Word.
